#!/bin/bash
# Downloads the pinned engines into Engines/bin/<arch>/, verifying each
# SHA-256 from its lock (Engines/goose.lock, Engines/opencode.lock).
# Binaries are never committed; the locks are the source of truth.
#   scripts/fetch-engines [arch|all] [--engine goose|opencode|all]   (default: this Mac, goose)
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
engines=(goose)
archs=()
while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
  case "$1" in
    --engine) shift; [[ "$1" == "all" ]] && engines=(goose opencode) || engines=("$1") ;;
    all) archs=(x86_64 arm64) ;;
    *) archs+=("$1") ;;
  esac
  shift
done
[[ ${#archs[@]} -eq 0 ]] && archs=("$(uname -m)")
# Every temporary folder is removed on exit (a trap set inside the loop would keep only the last).
temps=()
trap 'for t in "${temps[@]:-}"; do [[ -n "$t" ]] && rm -rf "$t"; done' EXIT
for engine in "${engines[@]}"; do
  lock="Engines/$engine.lock"
  [[ "$engine" == "goose" ]] && binary=goose-acp || binary=$(/usr/bin/plutil -extract binary raw -o - "$lock")
  for arch in "${archs[@]}"; do
    [[ "$arch" == "aarch64" ]] && arch=arm64
    url=$(/usr/bin/plutil -extract "assets.$arch.url" raw -o - "$lock")
    sum=$(/usr/bin/plutil -extract "assets.$arch.sha256" raw -o - "$lock")
    dest="Engines/bin/$arch"
    # A cached binary counts only if it's still the one installed: its own hash, recorded at install, must match.
    if [[ -x "$dest/$binary" ]] && [[ "$(cat "$dest/.$binary.sha256" 2>/dev/null)" == "$sum" ]] \
       && [[ "$(cat "$dest/.$binary.content" 2>/dev/null)" == "$(/usr/bin/shasum -a 256 "$dest/$binary" | cut -d' ' -f1)" ]]; then
      echo "$binary $arch: up to date"; continue
    fi
    tmp=$(mktemp -d); temps+=("$tmp")
    archive="$tmp/archive"
    /usr/bin/curl --fail --location --silent --show-error --output "$archive" "$url"
    actual=$(/usr/bin/shasum -a 256 "$archive" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    if [[ "$actual" != "$sum" ]]; then echo "$binary $arch: checksum mismatch ($actual)" >&2; exit 1; fi
    mkdir -p "$tmp/x"
    case "$url" in
      *.zip) /usr/bin/ditto -x -k "$archive" "$tmp/x" ;;
      *) /usr/bin/tar -xzf "$archive" -C "$tmp/x" ;;
    esac
    bin=$(find "$tmp/x" -type f -name "$binary" -perm -u+x | head -1)
    [[ -n "$bin" ]] || { echo "$binary $arch: binary not found in archive" >&2; exit 1; }
    mkdir -p "$dest"
    rm -f "$dest/$binary"
    mv "$bin" "$dest/$binary"
    echo "$sum" > "$dest/.$binary.sha256"
    /usr/bin/shasum -a 256 "$dest/$binary" | cut -d' ' -f1 > "$dest/.$binary.content"
    echo "$binary $arch: $(/usr/bin/plutil -extract version raw -o - "$lock") installed"
  done
done
